{"slug":"same-bst-orderings","title":"Other Orders That Build the Same Search Tree","topic":"trees","difficulty":"hard","order":579,"tags":["tree","bst","combinatorics","recursion","modular-arithmetic"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"The first number is the root; the two halves may be interleaved in any way","body":["Inserting the numbers of a list one by one into an empty binary search tree builds a tree. Different lists can build the **same** tree: the list `[2, 1, 3]` and the list `[2, 3, 1]` both give the root 2 with the children 1 and 3. How many lists (orderings of the same numbers) give exactly the same tree?","Look at the first number: it is the **root**, in every ordering that builds this tree. The numbers smaller than the root all go to the left subtree and the larger ones to the right subtree, and each subtree is built by its own numbers **in the order they appear**. The only freedom is how the left numbers and the right numbers are **interleaved**: any interleaving works, as long as each side keeps its own order (otherwise the shape inside a subtree would change).","If the left part has `a` numbers and the right part `b`, the number of interleavings is the binomial coefficient `C(a + b, a)`, and the two sides can be ordered independently inside. So:",{"code":"ways(list) = C(len(list) - 1, len(left)) * ways(left) * ways(right)\n   where left = the numbers smaller than list[0], right = the larger ones, both in the original order\nways(list with at most 2 numbers) = 1"},"The number of **other** orderings is `ways(list) - 1`. The result is large, so it is printed modulo 1000000007. The binomial coefficients come from Pascal's triangle modulo the same number: `C(i, j) = C(i - 1, j - 1) + C(i - 1, j)`. For `n` up to 800 the table has about 320000 entries, and the recursion has at most `n` levels."]},"statement":["The numbers of a list are inserted one by one, in the given order, into an initially empty binary search tree (a number smaller than a node goes to its left subtree, a larger one to its right subtree). How many other orderings of the same numbers build exactly the same tree? Print the answer modulo 1000000007."],"inputFormat":["The first line has `n`.","The second line has `n` different integers: the order in which the values are inserted into an empty binary search tree."],"outputFormat":["Print the number of other orderings modulo 1000000007."],"constraints":["1 <= n <= 800","-10^9 <= every value <= 10^9, and all values are different"],"examples":[{"input":"3\n2 1 3\n","output":"1\n","note":"Only [2, 3, 1] builds the same tree: 1."},{"input":"5\n3 4 5 1 2\n","output":"5\n","note":"The root 3 has the left part [1, 2] and the right part [4, 5]: C(4, 2) = 6 interleavings, so 6 - 1 = 5 other orderings."}],"hints":["The first number is the root of the tree in every such ordering.","Split the rest into the smaller and the larger numbers, keeping their order; the two halves are interleaved in C(a + b, a) ways.","Multiply by the answers of the two halves, subtract 1 at the end, and take everything modulo 1000000007."],"starter":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\nn = int(input())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> a[i];\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        long n = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long[] a = new long[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) a[i] = Long.parseLong(next());\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["The first number is the root; the smaller and the larger numbers (in their original order) form the two subtrees, which can be interleaved in C(a + b, a) ways. The answer is the product over all subtrees, minus one, modulo 1000000007."],"complexity":"Time O(n^2), space O(n^2) for Pascal's triangle.","code":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\nMOD = 1000000007\nC = [[1]]\nfor i in range(1, 801):\n    row = [1] * (i + 1)\n    for j in range(1, i):\n        row[j] = (C[i - 1][j - 1] + C[i - 1][j]) % MOD\n    C.append(row)\n\ndef ways(seq):\n    if len(seq) <= 2:\n        return 1\n    root = seq[0]\n    left = [x for x in seq if x < root]\n    right = [x for x in seq if x > root]\n    return C[len(seq) - 1][len(left)] * ways(left) % MOD * ways(right) % MOD\n\nn = int(input())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\nprint((ways(a) - 1) % MOD)\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst long long MOD = 1000000007LL;\nvector<vector<long long>> C;\n\nvoid buildTable() {\n    C.assign(801, vector<long long>());\n    C[0] = {1};\n    for (int i = 1; i <= 800; i++) {\n        C[i].assign(i + 1, 1);\n        for (int j = 1; j < i; j++) C[i][j] = (C[i - 1][j - 1] + C[i - 1][j]) % MOD;\n    }\n}\n\nlong long ways(const vector<long long>& seq) {\n    if (seq.size() <= 2) return 1;\n    vector<long long> left, right;\n    for (long long x : seq) {\n        if (x < seq[0]) left.push_back(x);\n        else if (x > seq[0]) right.push_back(x);\n    }\n    return C[seq.size() - 1][left.size()] * ways(left) % MOD * ways(right) % MOD;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> a[i];\n\n    buildTable();\n    cout << (ways(a) - 1 + MOD) % MOD << \"\\n\";\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    static final long MOD = 1000000007L;\n    static long[][] C = new long[801][];\n\n    static void buildTable() {\n        C[0] = new long[] {1};\n        for (int i = 1; i <= 800; i++) {\n            C[i] = new long[i + 1];\n            Arrays.fill(C[i], 1);\n            for (int j = 1; j < i; j++) C[i][j] = (C[i - 1][j - 1] + C[i - 1][j]) % MOD;\n        }\n    }\n\n    static long ways(List<Long> seq) {\n        if (seq.size() <= 2) return 1;\n        List<Long> left = new ArrayList<>(), right = new ArrayList<>();\n        long root = seq.get(0);\n        for (long x : seq) {\n            if (x < root) left.add(x);\n            else if (x > root) right.add(x);\n        }\n        return C[seq.size() - 1][left.size()] * ways(left) % MOD * ways(right) % MOD;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        long n = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long[] a = new long[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) a[i] = Long.parseLong(next());\n\n        buildTable();\n        List<Long> seq = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (long x : a) seq.add(x);\n        System.out.println((ways(seq) - 1 + MOD) % MOD);\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"3\n2 1 3\n","output":"1\n"},{"input":"5\n3 4 5 1 2\n","output":"5\n"},{"input":"1\n7\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"2\n1 2\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"3\n1 2 3\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"10\n-803150137 221322873 197761981 489643844 404553601 -384844438 452409622 -580889113 -124729421 -678984281\n","output":"167\n"},{"input":"40\n965926610 -632249336 -717194711 -248965872 194675554 953099948 69613437 -267809960 139267175 775712357 -194959685 305581280 507808018 -174326644 -767306640 -677056110 -103631377 437045821 -827821856 -485090480 359966034 -789502482 843457483 -385363463 712417270 -606115013 -706489752 -296088398 -555621283 -432760441 -726934767 -884675707 724065006 -575192443 -625179015 -156635009 558666013 207130817 -69273856 733681747\n","output":"103705907\n"},{"input":"120\n757269136 -960907537 764487508 -895119058 495437441 -490479328 -589014472 -444830573 511427499 997454973 -503780325 991028063 660681722 -210175640 597059155 -772816100 499028437 479426896 81559709 752200461 668297765 -538600339 -812784053 -901431521 -676685853 -725745152 -695199567 -778637206 345792911 -218155953 426920827 58818102 457010519 556219331 -881510713 78413930 830641985 -582768627 -336730455 405499118 -84919277 431933546 229304010 -556552393 324614365 -517313856 -190771490 -850743894 123630087 444066975 -70008469 267941951 218255740 -97895413 769699200 -381871903 318733080 238431946 -237092013 631112614 -844331005 885773445 -571185450 -912806967 -911383610 295761274 924311723 -540651074 -803275345 -489583884 753604872 -657386058 624606507 866237219 986780920 750402863 109596205 996811759 -388110135 5439323 582837131 -739897645 -860178242 -213600129 546667119 377798702 191754688 734473120 -695107391 -538347441 454332651 -798488996 -454118010 805217591 -282706792 -112638897 -520579128 -970554731 892486617 -307408460 398179804 729811541 -732524355 740421172 759286063 -751138352 70515161 716386023 369403890 463565565 789170432 -404914761 246403623 -517544288 83660130 -583181513 -585191720 441212454 761901992 -122366387\n","output":"173048040\n"},{"input":"400\n-100224717 585027373 -232849339 -940099552 -951167569 864204482 -673500799 592755253 -959852080 -761934256 51003426 -533713633 5